{
  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with multi-profile and PCA_n2000 (config_002, avgpool) is the best result so far at 0.591 acc / 0.573 F1, a large jump over single-profile RNA (config_001, 0.485) and far above image-only (config_010, 0.208). This confirms RNA is the dominant modality and that multi-profile aggregation adds substantial signal. However, we have only tested one aggregation strategy (avgpool). Question: config_003 isolates the effect of aggregation method by swapping avgpool → transformer while holding every other factor (RNA-only, multi-profile, PCA_n2000) constant relative to config_002. This is a clean, controlled comparison that tells us whether learned attention-based aggregation can further improve on simple averaging, or whether avgpool is already near the ceiling for this encoder. Why best next step: it is the most direct exploitation of the strongest result (config_002) while probing an untested design dimension. If transformer significantly outperforms avgpool, subsequent experiments can pair the better aggregator with alternative encoders (scvi, scGPT); if the gain is marginal, we learn that aggregation is not the bottleneck and should pivot to encoder choice. Under a limited budget, this single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the aggregation axis before committing to more complex multimodal or encoder-variation experiments."
}

